parts":[{"text":"து","lemma":"து","gloss":"it"}],"gloss":"it is"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"Closely-knit garland-wearing bamboo-like large shoulders-having / sea-bathing women in the seaside grove built / small house united friendship, O friend! / one day the lord of the shore if he abandons, / many days coming pain-nature-it-indeed.","translation":"O friend! The love that began in the little toy house built in the seaside grove by girls with bamboo-like shoulders wearing closely-knit garlands as they bathed in the sea—if the lord of the shore leaves us for even a single day, it brings many days of deep sorrow.","modern":"தோழியே! நெருக்கமாகத் தொடுக்கப்பட்ட மாலைகளையும் மூங்கில் போன்ற பெரிய தோள்களையும் உடைய பெண்கள், கடலில் நீராடிவிட்டு கடற்கரைச் சோலையில் கட்டிய சிறிய மணல் வீட்டில் உண்டான நம் நட்பு, இத்துறைமுகத் தலைவன் ஒரு நாள் நம்மைப் பிரிந்தாலும், பல நாட்களுக்குத் துன்பத்தைத் தருவதாகும்.","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her confidante when the hero delays their marriage or leaves her for a short period. She expresses how intense her love is, explaining that even a single day's separation from the lord of the maritime tract causes her prolonged, agonizing pain. The poem is set in the neytal (maritime) landscape, where the sea and shore form the backdrop. The image of the 'small house' built by the sea-bathing women represents the fragile, temporary nature of their secret meetings, contrasting with the enduring pain of separation. Key words include 'naṭpu' (friendship/love), 'tuṟaivaṉ' (lord of the shore), and 'iṉṉāmai' (pain).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.9],[1.06,1.5],[1.5,2.0],[2.0,2.35],[2.35,2.7],[2.7,2.86],[2.86,3.8],[3.8,4.55],[4.55,5.3],[5.3,5.54],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,6.6],[6.6,7.12],[7.12,7.5],[7.5,8.15],[8.15,8.56],[8.56,8.86],[8.86,9.17]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.17],[1.32,1.75],[1.75,2.2],[2.2,2.6],[2.6,3.0],[3.0,3.16],[3.16,4.1],[4.1,5.26],[5.2